<!--
  PRODUCT_SPEC 3.1 — Norwegian Bokmål.

  `app_name` is deliberately absent: the product is called ShelfPlayer in every locale, and a
  translated launcher label would be a different app on the home screen.

  Two conventions worth stating, because they are what a reviewer should check rather than the
  individual words:

  - **Bokmål, not Nynorsk**, and the moderate register a Norwegian reader expects from software:
    "logg på" rather than "innlogging", "server" rather than "tjener".
  - **Sentence case throughout.** Norwegian does not capitalise mid-sentence words the way English
    headings do, so "Continue listening" is "Fortsett å lytte" and not "Fortsett Å Lytte".

  Plurals declare `one` and `other`, which is the set Norwegian needs — it splits on exactly one, as
  English does.
-->
